    "final_answer": "I have found the answer. Based on my research using ronaldostats.app, a dedicated statistics site for Cristiano Ronaldo, here are the findings:\n\n## Answer: Cristiano Ronaldo's Most Goals in a Single Season\n\nCristiano Ronaldo scored his most goals in a single season in **2014/15**, with **61 goals** for Real Madrid across all competitions (54 appearances). This is officially the peak of his club career.\n\n### Key Details:\n- **Best Club Season**: **2014/15** with **61 goals** for Real Madrid\n- **Best Calendar Year**: **2013** with **69 goals** (across both Real Madrid and Portugal)\n\n### Top 5 Calendar Years (per ronaldostats.app):\n| Year | Goals |\n|------|-------|\n| 2013 | **69** ⭐ |\n| 2012 | 63 |\n| 2014 | 61 |\n| 2011 | 60 |\n| 2015 | 57 |\n\n### Top Season Goals by Club (Real Madrid era, 2009–2018):\n- 2009/10: 33\n- 2010/11: 53\n- 2011/12: 60\n- 2012/13: 55\n- 2013/14: 51\n- **2014/15: 61** ⭐ (peak)\n- 2015/16: 51\n- 2016/17: 42\n- 2017/18: 44\n\nSo depending on how you define \"single season\":\n- **By club season**: **2014/15** with **61 goals** at Real Madrid\n- **By calendar year**: **2013** with **69 goals** total",
